    <div class="practitioners" style="grid-template-columns:1fr;max-width:640px;margin-left:auto;margin-right:auto;">
      <div class="practitioner-card reveal">
        <img src="/img/Ssq.jpg" alt="My portrait" class="practitioner-photo">
        <div class="practitioner-role">Qigong &amp; Raja Yoga</div>
                <p class="practitioner-bio">I have over two decades of training in Asian healing arts. I have practised Yoga since 1997, studying with masters in Japan and India, and I am a certified Yoga teacher through IYF Asia, qualified in South Korea. Since 2010 I have trained intensively in authentic Qigong, studying and practising with masters across Mainland China, Hong Kong, Japan, Indonesia, Thailand and Scotland. I am also a certified Therapeutic Thai bodywork therapist and instructor, accredited by TTMA Japan since 2018, with deep additional study in TCM Reflexology. I have taught at senior tutor level at the Traditional Thai Massage Association Japan and at the Shivaga Traditional Medical School in Japan, where I delivered Therapeutic Thai Bodywork, Reflexology and Qigong. My understanding of Qi cultivation, the principles of Traditional Chinese Medicine as they relate to energy work, and hands-on therapeutic bodywork informs every session I teach. Beyond the realm of practice and teaching, I am an initiate and direct disciple in the Inchegiri Navnath Sampradaya lineage (Nisargadatta Maharaj, Ramakant Maharaj).</p>
      </div>
